# Hitchens's Case Against Censorship

This is a reconstruction of Christopher Hitchens's debate speech arguing against censorship and hate speech laws. His central claim is that speech should never be censored, supported by multiple independent arguments.

## Core Claims

[No Censorship Ever]: Speech should never be censored, regardless of content or potential harm.

[Audience Right to Hear]: The audience's right to hear is as important as the speaker's right to speak.

[Heretic Value]: Dissenting minority views are especially valuable and must be protected.

[No Trusted Censor]: No person or institution can be trusted with the authority to determine what speech should be censored.

[Unpredictable Harm]: It is impossible to know in advance what speech will cause harm.

[Religion Main Hate Source]: Religion and organized religion are the main sources of hatred in the world.

[Religion Seeks Protection]: Religious groups seek hate speech protection while promoting hatred themselves.

## Foundational Arguments

<Milton Argument>
(1) Milton, Paine, and Mill establish that free speech is not just about the speaker.
(2) Every time you silence somebody, you make yourself a prisoner of your own action.
(3) You deny yourself the right to hear something.
(4) The right of everyone in the audience to listen is equally involved.
----
(5) [Audience Right to Hear]

<Milton Argument>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<Mill Heretic Argument>
(1) If all society agreed on one proposition except one person, that one heretic should be heard.
(2) It becomes MORE important to hear the heretic precisely because of the consensus.
(3) We benefit from even outrageous or appalling views.
(4) Rosa Luxemburg said freedom of speech is meaningless unless it means the freedom of the person who thinks differently.
----
(5) [Heretic Value]

<Mill Heretic Argument>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<Holocaust Denier Example>
(1) If everyone is taught one official story of the Holocaust.
(2) And one person denies it happened.
(3) That person's right to speak must be given EXTRA protection.
(4) What they say took effort to formulate.
(5) It might contain a grain of historical truth however unlikely.
(6) It makes people question how do I know what I think I know.
----
(7) [Heretic Value]

<Holocaust Denier Example>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

## Authority Problems

<Authority Argument>
(1) Censorship requires someone to decide what speech is harmful.
(2) This decision maker must be trusted with authority over others access to ideas.
(3) To whom would you give this job?
(4) Do you know anyone worthy of deciding what you can read or hear?
(5) No one in the audience raised their hand to nominate someone.
----
(6) [No Trusted Censor]

<Authority Argument>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<Dr Johnson Argument>
(1) Dr Johnson compiled the first great English dictionary.
(2) Respectable ladies congratulated him for excluding indecent words.
(3) Dr Johnson replied: Ladies I congratulate you on being able to look them up.
(4) The ladies had searched through the dictionary specifically looking for filthy words.
----
(5) Those who seek to censor are often seeking the content they claim to suppress.
(6) One has to suspect the motives of those who are determined to be offended.

<Dr Johnson Argument>
  -> [No Trusted Censor]

<Holmes Misuse Argument>
(1) Oliver Wendell Holmes created the fire in a crowded theater standard.
(2) He used this to jail Yiddish speaking socialists.
(3) They opposed Wilson's entry into WWI in a language most Americans could not read.
(4) They were refugees from the war they were trying to prevent.
(5) The socialists could be seen as the real firefighters warning of genuine danger.
----
(6) The supposedly wise Holmes misused censorship power.
(7) Who is to decide who is really shouting fire when there is real fire.

<Holmes Misuse Argument>
  -> [No Trusted Censor]

<Man For All Seasons>
(1) Thomas More argued with a witch hunting prosecutor.
(2) Prosecutor said I would cut down every law in England to capture the devil.
(3) More replied when the devil turned to meet you where would you run for protection.
(4) All the laws having been cut down and flattened who would protect you then.
----
(5) Every time you violate free speech of someone else you make a rod for your own back.

<Man For All Seasons>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<David Irving Defense>
(1) David Irving is a British historian imprisoned in Austria.
(2) Imprisoned not for what he said but for potentially planning to say something.
(3) Austria gave us Kurt Waldheim and Jorg Haider and presumes to judge historical truth.
(4) Austria convinced the world Hitler was German and Beethoven was Viennese.
----
(5) Even in the hardest case of Holocaust denial censorship is wrong.

<David Irving Defense>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

## Epistemological Problems

<Epistemology Argument>
(1) Harm from speech depends on timing location audience circumstances and tone.
(2) These contextual factors cannot be known or predicted in advance.
(3) Prior restraint requires knowing in advance what will cause harm.
(4) In the US prior restraint is banned by the First Amendment.
(5) No one has the knowledge that would be required to make that call.
----
(6) [Unpredictable Harm]

<Epistemology Argument>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<Fire Theater Context>
(1) Who decides who is really warning of fire versus falsely alarming.
(2) The Yiddish socialists could claim they were warning of real danger.
(3) The context determines whether fire is warning or panic inducing.
----
(4) Harm from speech depends entirely on context which cannot be predetermined.

<Fire Theater Context>
  -> [Unpredictable Harm]

## Religion Paradox

<Religion Paradox>
(1) [Religion Main Hate Source]
(2) How will censorship advocates ban religion.
(3) How will they stop expression of religious loathing hatred and bigotry.
(4) They cannot because religion is protected expression.
----
(5) [Religion Seeks Protection]
(6) The main source of hatred seeks protection from censorship.
(7) This creates a fundamental paradox for hate speech laws.

<Bible Incitement>
(1) The Bible says you have to hate homosexuals.
(2) If Falwell says this because the Bible says so he is right about what the Bible says.
(3) This might make people use violence.
(4) What are you going to do about that.
(5) Religious people will say do not put your hands on our Bible or we will call the hate speech police.
----
(6) Religious texts incite hatred and violence.
(7) You cannot ban religion.

<Bible Incitement>
  -> <Religion Paradox>

<Christianity Anti-Semitism>
(1) Kristallnacht was not the result of 10 years of Jew baiting.
(2) It was the result of 2000 years of Christianity.
(3) Based on one verse of St John's Gospel.
(4) This led to pogroms after every Easter sermon for hundreds of years.
(5) The verse claims Jews demanded Christ's blood on themselves and all their children.
----
(6) This is the warrant and license for anti Jewish pogroms.
(7) What are you going to do about that.
(8) You cannot censor St John's Gospel.

<Christianity Anti-Semitism>
  -> <Religion Paradox>

<Warrant for Oppression>
(1) Look for the warrant for slavery subjection of women burning homosexuals ethnic cleansing anti-Semitism.
(2) You look no further than a famous book that is on every pulpit.
(3) This book is in every synagogue and in every mosque.
----
(4) Religious texts incite hatred and oppression.
(5) The force that is the main source of hatred is also the main caller for censorship.

<Warrant for Oppression>
  -> <Religion Paradox>

<Evolution of Religion>
(1) Religious belief is ineradicable as long as we remain stupid poorly evolved mammals.
(2) Our prefrontal lobes are too small and our adrenaline glands are too big.
(3) We are afraid of the dark and afraid to die.
(4) We believe truths of holy books that are so stupid a child can see through them.
(5) No Canadian law will solve this evolutionary problem.
----
(6) Religion should be treated with ridicule and hatred and contempt.
(7) And I claim that right.

<Evolution of Religion>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

## Islam Specific Arguments

[Islam Special Threat]: Islam currently poses a serious menace to freedoms beyond just speech.

[Islam Dual Position]: Islam is globally powerful but poses as a vulnerable minority in Western societies.

<Islam Irony>
(1) Not all monotheisms are the same at the moment.
(2) [Islam Special Threat]
(3) Globally Islam is powerful controls oil wealth and large countries.
(4) It pumps Wahhabism worldwide poisoning societies ruining minds of children.
(5) Training people in violence making a cult of death and suicide and murder.
(6) [Islam Dual Position]
(7) In Western societies Islam poses as a cringing minority deserving protection.
----
(8) The religion that most threatens speech freedom seeks the most speech protection.
(9) This is the ultimate irony of hate speech laws.

<Islam Irony>
  -> <Religion Paradox>

<Prophet Criticism>
(1) Islam claims final revelation through an archangel to one illiterate businessman.
(2) The resulting material is largely plagiarized from the Old and New Testament.
(3) It should be accepted as divine revelation and final and unalterable.
(4) Those who do not accept are fit to be treated as cattle infidels slaves and victims.
(5) I do not think Muhammad ever heard those voices.
(6) I am more likely objectively correct than the traditional account.
----
(7) But who is the one under threat.
(8) The person who promotes unverifiable claims gets protection.
(9) The person who says this is silly enough to cartoon faces threats.

<Prophet Criticism>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]

<Cartoon Controversy>
(1) I say Islam is silly enough to cartoon.
(2) Response is placards saying behead those who cartoon Islam in London Toronto New York.
(3) These threateners do not get arrested for hate speech.
(4) I might get in trouble for criticizing Muhammad.
----
(5) Where are your priorities.
(6) You are giving away what is most precious without a fight.
(7) You are praising people who want to deny you the right to resist.

<Cartoon Controversy>
  -> <Islam Irony>

## The False Antithesis

<False Antithesis>
(1) The main source of hatred is religion.
(2) Religion is also the main caller for censorship.
(3) Hate speech laws would protect the primary sources of hatred.
(4) You cannot ban religious speech so laws will be selectively enforced.
(5) Those who threaten violence seek hate speech protection for their views.
----
(6) You are faced with a gigantic false antithesis.
(7) The question is not free speech versus protection from hate.
(8) It is free speech versus protecting hatred while suppressing criticism of it.

<False Antithesis>
  -> [No Censorship Ever]
